        "title": "Stratification and Inequality",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Social stratification is **the structural ranking of social groups in a hierarchy of unequal access to valued resources** — income, wealth, power, status, education, health. Unlike individual differences in resources, stratification is systematic, institutionalized, and transmitted across generations."
    }
